    {
      "skill_id": "de-a1-003",
      "title": "Questions with question words",
      "explanation": "A question word opens the question, the finite verb comes second and the subject follows: Wo wohnst du? Frequent question words are wer (who), was (what), wo (where), woher (from where), wohin (to where), wann (when), wie (how) and warum (why). Questions with a question word are answered with information, not with ja or nein. Wie heißt du? means 'What is your name?'",
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Wo wohnst du?",
          "en": "Where do you live?"
        },
        {
          "de": "Woher kommt Anna?",
          "en": "Where does Anna come from?"
        },
        {
          "de": "Was lernt ihr?",
          "en": "What are you (all) learning?"
        }
      ],
